course: dictionary
lesson: 11717
title: Proving it is real
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a hard word from the words around it. Look at this: «The expert will authenticate the old painting before the museum buys it.» Before a museum buys something, someone has to check that it is real, so authenticate must mean to prove something is genuine.
explain: The word can also be about people. «To open the app, you must authenticate with your fingerprint.» The app checks who you are before it lets you in. Try your meaning in the sentence: does "check who you are" fit? Then it is a good guess.
explain: Look at the word family. Authentication is the name for the checking process: «Two-factor authentication asks for a password and a code sent to your phone.» Authentic means real or genuine, the opposite of fake. When you know one word in a family, you can often guess the others.
fact: Authenticate is a verb: you authenticate, she authenticates, they authenticated, and authenticating is the -ing form.
fact: «Authenticate» means to prove that something is real or genuine, not fake.
fact: In computing, «authenticate» means to check someone's identity before letting them in, for example with a password or fingerprint.
fact: «Two-factor authentication» uses two checks, such as a password and a code, to make sure it really is you.
fact: Experts authenticate old paintings and coins to show they are real, not copies.
exercise: «The expert will authenticate the old painting before the museum buys it.» What does authenticate mean here? | To hang it on the wall | *To prove the painting is real | To paint a copy of it | To sell it quickly
exercise: Mia's tablet asks her to authenticate with her fingerprint. What is it checking? | How fast she can type | What colour her tablet is | Whether she likes games | *Who she is, before letting her in
exercise: «Only an authentic coin is worth that price.» Find and copy the word that means real or genuine. | price | *authentic | coin | worth
test: «Two-factor authentication asks for a password and a code sent to your phone.» Why does the app ask for two things? | To send a message to your friends | To use up more battery | To make the password longer | *To make sure it really is you
test: Which word means real, the opposite of fake? | invented | forged | copied | *authentic
exam: Dad says the bank will authenticate a payment before it goes through. What does authenticate mean? | *Check that it is genuine and allowed | Write it down in a book | Pay it twice | Cancel the bank account
